  "question": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0075_9b20cf4bd673.png\" style=\"width: 167px; height: 120px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>In the above reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of toluene is converted into benzaldehyde with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>92</mn><mo>%</mo></math> yield. The amount of benzaldehyde produced is____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "530",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0075_8346b2fde989.png\" style=\"width: 336px; height: 158px;\" /></p><p>Molar mass of benzaldehyde=<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>106</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>Number of moles of toluene&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>92</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Number&nbsp;of moles of Benzaldehyde&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>92</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Mass of Benzaldehyde&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>92</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>106</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>530</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
